  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Transitioning the Neotree Project in Zimbabwe to National Ownership:Integrating and Scaling Neotree within the Health System.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Neonatal mortality remains a critical challenge in Zimbabwe; one of the few countries in Africa where this metric has worsened over the last decade.  Resource challenges, such as a lack of trained staff are ongoing, and it is reasonable to assume these trends could continue given the upheaval in development policy and disruptions in the wider global economy.  Whilst the MoHCC is actively rolling out the Impilo EHR nationwide to primary health clinics (PHC), specialised neonatal workflows are required to manage complex newborn care effectively. Neotree has demonstrated clinical success, but keeping it as a standalone, donor-dependent application limits its long-term viability. To ensure lasting and widescale impact, Neotree must be absorbed into the sovereign digital infrastructure (Impilo for PHCs, and Impilo vNEXT for hospitals), and the MoHCC workforce must be equipped to govern, maintain, and utilise the system independently.</narrative>
  </description>
